WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.782
Sign Bridge explores an interface for American Sign Language.

00:00:04.782 --> 00:00:09.285
This release does not recognize signs or translate conversations.

00:00:09.285 --> 00:00:13.287
It demonstrates local preview and a confirmation-and-correction workflow.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.789
The camera starts off.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:19.560
A short local video can be previewed without uploading it.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.823
Size and duration limits are explicit.

00:00:21.823 --> 00:00:25.217
Previewing a clip does not analyze or translate it.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.225
I open the prewritten scenario.

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:30.560
Hello appears as an example suggestion.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.786
It was not inferred from a gesture, and the banner explicitly identifies it as not AI

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:37.175
output.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.689
I reject the suggestion.

00:00:39.689 --> 00:00:43.107
The interface confirms that no meaning was assumed.

00:00:43.107 --> 00:00:49.088
The person communicating stays in control instead of being forced to accept an interpretation.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.066
I type Please write your reply and add it to the walkthrough.

00:00:54.066 --> 00:00:56.108
The text stays in this page.

00:00:56.108 --> 00:00:57.811
Ending the walkthrough clears it;

00:00:57.811 --> 00:01:00.875
this is a manual correction, not an ASL translation.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.467
The library lists the remaining work:

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:08.945
an evaluated model and authorized full-phrase videos reviewed in ASL.

00:01:08.945 --> 00:01:10.736
Neither is available yet.

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:16.109
This is an interface prototype with visible boundaries, not a working interpreter.
